What’s Driving the Market
•	Electric-vehicle adoption: Global EV sales increased by 35% year over year in 2023, strengthening demand for water-based binders capable of supporting high-performance lithium-ion electrodes.
•	Growing SBR-adhered battery installations: The installed base of SBR-adhered lithium batteries is expanding at approximately 8% annually, according to the report, as EV and energy-storage manufacturers seek mechanical integrity and durability.
•	Raw-material and formulation dynamics: Butadiene and styrene precursor prices can fluctuate by 15–25% per quarter, encouraging suppliers to diversify sourcing, improve formulation efficiency and strengthen supply-chain resilience.
Chemical Industry Pulse
The battery-materials industry is undergoing a transition toward formulations that combine performance, manufacturing efficiency and lower environmental impact. Water-based binder systems are receiving increased attention as battery producers seek alternatives to solvent-intensive processing while maintaining electrode cohesion and cycle stability. Within this environment, polymer suppliers are working on formulations compatible with higher energy-density electrodes, silicon-based anodes and emerging battery architectures. The growing overlap between chemical companies and battery manufacturers is also changing the competitive landscape, with co-development and long-term supply relationships becoming increasingly important. Meanwhile, raw-material volatility remains a central issue for polymer producers, particularly where butadiene and styrene prices move rapidly. These trends are encouraging greater supply-chain diversification, localized production and application-specific binder development across Asia-Pacific, Europe and North America.
Segmentation Highlights
•	By Type: Emulsion SBR (e-SBR) and Solution SBR (s-SBR). Emulsion SBR leads because of water-based processing, lower VOC emissions, robust adhesion and established high-volume production.
•	By Application: Electric Vehicles, Consumer Electronics, Industrial Energy Storage and Grid Storage Solutions. Electric Vehicles are the dominant growth application.
•	By End User: Battery Cell Manufacturers, Battery Pack Assemblers and Automotive OEMs. Battery Cell Manufacturers drive demand because SBR is directly applied during electrode slurry preparation.
•	By Binder Function: Active Material Binder, Conductive Agent Binder and Multi-Functional Binder. Active Material Binder is the foundational segment.
•	By Electrode Chemistry: Graphite Anodes, Silicon-Based Anodes and Next-Generation Anodes. Graphite Anodes currently dominate, while silicon-based and next-generation chemistries are creating new formulation requirements.
Regional Outlook
•	Asia-Pacific: Identified as the leading region, supported by its concentration of lithium-ion battery production and integrated supply chains.
•	Asia-Pacific production base: The region contributes more than 70% of global lithium-ion production, providing a substantial manufacturing ecosystem for SBR binders.
•	North America: Identified as the emerging region, with growth linked to expanding EV production and large-scale energy-storage projects.
•	Europe: Demand is being supported by green-industry policies, stringent safety standards and interest in lower-environmental-impact battery materials.
